Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-01
Subject: Avoid packed aggregate access hazards in the translated bootstrap
License: expat

tp2cc intentionally rejects or guards references that would bind C++
references through packed subobjects.  FPC 2.6.0 has two different cases:

- packed records that are real serialized/on-disk formats and must stay
  packed (`tsettings` in PPUs and PE/COFF headers);
- packed records that are only in-memory compiler tables and can be
  depacked for the bootstrap.

For serialized packed records, preserve the layout and route the access
through safe carriers:
- copy the nested `current_settings.alignment` / `init_settings.alignment`
  subrecord before reading or updating its fields;
- use an explicit typed pointer carrier for PE optional-header
  `DataDirectory` indexing.

For in-memory-only metadata, remove unnecessary packing:
- `compiler/i386/daopt386.pas`: depack optimizer `TContent`;
- `compiler/x86/aasmcpu.pas`: depack `TInsProp` and `tinsentry`.

This does not change PPU or object-file formats.  It only avoids forming
misaligned references in the C++ bootstrap for places where the Pascal
source used nested or indexed access through packed aggregate fields.

--- a/compiler/globals.pas
+++ b/compiler/globals.pas
@@ -1359,8 +1359,14 @@
 
 
     function var_align(want_align: longint): shortint;
+      var
+        alignment : talignmentinfo;
       begin
-        var_align := used_align(want_align,current_settings.alignment.varalignmin,current_settings.alignment.varalignmax);
+        { tsettings is packed because it is serialized into PPUs; copy the
+          subrecord before accessing its members so the bootstrap translator
+          does not have to form nested references into a packed aggregate. }
+        alignment := current_settings.alignment;
+        var_align := used_align(want_align,alignment.varalignmin,alignment.varalignmax);
       end;
 
 
@@ -1372,8 +1378,13 @@
 
 
     function const_align(want_align: longint): shortint;
+      var
+        alignment : talignmentinfo;
       begin
-        const_align := used_align(want_align,current_settings.alignment.constalignmin,current_settings.alignment.constalignmax);
+        { Keep tsettings packed for PPU serialization; avoid chained access
+          through the packed alignment field. }
+        alignment := current_settings.alignment;
+        const_align := used_align(want_align,alignment.constalignmin,alignment.constalignmax);
       end;
 
 
